quran[5]{c,v,t}:
  5,32,"For this reason, We prescribed for the Children of Israel that whoever kills a soul, without it being (a lawful punishment) for another soul or (a lawful punishment for spreading) disorder in the land, it is as if he has killed all humanity. And whoever saves a life, it is as if he has saved all humanity. Indeed, Our messengers came to them with clear signs; even after that, many of them continued transgressing in the land."
  5,33,"Indeed, the penalty for those who wage war against Allah and His Messenger (blessings and peace be upon him) and try to cause corruption (and disorder) in the land (by perpetrating robbery, bloodshed and terrorism) is that they should be (lawfully) awarded capital punishment, or they should be crucified, or their hands and feet should be (lawfully) struck off from opposite sides, or they should be (lawfully) imprisoned (or banished from the land). That is their disgrace in this world, and there is a terrible punishment for them in the Hereafter."
  5,34,"Except those who repent before you overpower them; then know that Allah is Most-Forgiving, All-Merciful."
  5,35,"O believers! Be conscious of Allah, seek the means that bring you closer to Him, and strive hard in His way, so that you may be prosperous."
  5,36,"Indeed, if the disbelievers were to possess everything on the earth and twice over (and offer it all) to ransom themselves from the punishment of the Day of Resurrection, it shall not be accepted from them. And there will be a painful punishment for them."
